one independently placed calibration row is exactly v.  The target digits are
the matrix-vector product, with B chosen large enough to prevent carries.
Consequently the calibration target digit is S=sum(v_i*lambda_i).  In every
other row, b_r=u_r*S+K*lambda_i, so one exact subtraction and division recovers
the matched multiplicity.  Claim 2 then produces the full cone certificate.
At n=40 this route, including the filler, uses at most 162 exact operations.

