magnitude, scale and spike row, so rank/magnitude outliers do not reveal them.
A scalar largest-first greedy ignores base digits and fails.  Random canonical
certificates face an injective map and fail.  The in-context spike-only ansatz
divides target digits by the spike but omits the shared rank-one component and
