codex
The successful `easy` replies exposed a weakness the generic probes missed: all three models recovered the direct one-spike-per-row coefficients in under a minute. I’m hardening the same paper-native construction by replacing that diagonal spike pattern with a randomly relabelled odd-cycle incidence pattern. It preserves inverse generation and exact verification, raises the mechanical dense solve, and still has a sub-300-operation route via the odd-cycle invariant.
apply patch
