codex
Implemented a native Track B Point-in-Cone generator based on Section 3, Claims 1–2 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2307.00406v1).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2307_00406.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/gen_2307_00406.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2307.00406/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass:

- Exact canonical density: `1 / 31^41`; random guessing: `0/200,000`.
- Four attacks: `0/8` successes each.
- Dense reference algorithm: 96,965 exact operations.
- Verified compact odd-cycle route: 248 operations.
- Answer: at most 888 characters and 166 atomic elements over 10,000 measured seeds.
- Relabelling invariance and doubled-size generation pass.

The mandatory oracle certification remains externally blocked: all bare, hinted, and placebo calls received HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded`, so `.meta.json` correctly contains no hardening verdict. The README records this explicitly; the API errors are not represented as model failures.
